      "content": "a system crash? i don't know if that's even possible without everything else breaking too. i just feel like the logic is fundamentally flawed. if the system is running a process that serves no purpose and only consumes resources, isn't the most efficient move to just terminate the thread? it feels like the only way to actually stop the cycle.",
